#
# Security region: cpu, hardened
#
# Speculation, control flow and the isolation the processor offers between
# kernel and user. sec_baseline compiles the vulnerability mitigations in,
# and the processor picks at boot the ones it needs; this region turns on
# what is off for every machine because it costs on every machine, which is
# why profile/latency took indirect branch tracking out.
#
#   sec_cpu_hardened   indirect branch tracking (every indirect call lands on
#                      an endbr64 or the processor stops it), call depth
#                      tracking for the Skylake generation's return buffer
#                      underflow, straight-line speculation barriers, user
#                      shadow stacks for programs that ask for one, and the
#                      transactional memory extension off
#   sec_cpu_locked     everything above, and the mitigations run at their
#                      strongest whatever the processor claims: page table
#                      isolation on every part, every vulnerable-or-not
#                      sibling thread off, microcode-assisted buffer clearing
#                      always
#
# The architecture's lines are in sec_cpu_hardened.x64 (and .arm). A region
# profile for an architecture that has nothing to add is just this file.
#
#> includes sec_baseline
